            <summary><h3>What is ActivePulse on NordicTrack and ProForm?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              An iFIT feature that adjusts speed and incline automatically to keep you in a heart-rate zone, using a Bluetooth heart-rate monitor sold separately. It needs an iFIT membership: the listings name iFIT Pro on the Commercial 1750 and iFIT Train on the Carbon TL.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do I need a subscription for heart-rate training on a treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Horizon, Sole and LifeSmart treadmills run heart-rate programs from the console with no membership. Only iFIT's automatic ActivePulse feature on NordicTrack and ProForm needs one.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can I use my Apple Watch as the treadmill heart rate monitor?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On some machines. Horizon's table lists Apple Watch and GymKit support for the 7.0 AT but not the 7.4 or 7.8. Watches also tend to lag behind a chest strap during intervals.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

